Z||000019||Spyder||11-01-2001||10:38 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/m9.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/m8.jpg">  <BR>Here is how my sub install is coming along; the one I started ooo soooo long ago.<BR>It consists of two Sony 12s and two Sony 5.25” in the center. Also in the lower doors is another pair of 5.25”s. I’ll have more pics eventually.<P>Those are some great looking installs! I always love seeing how people come up with new and interesting ways of doing installs. Looks Great Guys!<P><p>[This message has been edited by Spyder (edited 11-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||JetroGT||11-02-2001||06:40 AM||||I miss having a nice system in my car. Due to the amount of crack heads in Fort Worth I took it out. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/daily_system.jpg"> <BR>Now it sits in my closet with the rest of my fiero parts.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCP_0347.JPG"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DCP_0348.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000021||fieronv||11-02-2001||10:46 AM||||The amps run just fine even in the heat of the summer and having a black car. There is still some air circulation even in the front compartment. I've been running amps in the front for 6 years with no problems.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero2_WEB_1.jpg">   <BR>85GT (twoloud)||||reg||1
Z||000022||GodSend||11-02-2001||12:03 PM||||The newer PSOnes run off an external transformer. It is the type there the plug that plugs into the wall has a large box, and there is only a normal barrel type connect to go to the Unit.<P>Because of this, Sony makes a plug in adapter for the car (which is very small).  The nice thing about this is that you do not have to modify the powersupply, and you can easily take it out and play it in your house (I plan on removing it for the winter when I store it).  Instead of plugging the car adapter into the factory plug I bought a AUX plug from Canadian tire and wired it under the dash hidden away (easy to do.. just ground it, and hook up the possive to radio fuse in the fuse box).<P>The LCD was bought from partsexpress.com||||reg||1
Z||000023||Brandon86SE||11-02-2001||12:27 PM||||Hey Flashy, when did you do that?  Damn, been too long since I've been out to a Fiero meeting, I guess.  I'm doing pretty much the same, but with the amp behind the driver's side.  I'll post pics when it's done.  The sub box is currently in a couple pieces at my friends house, we're in the middle of cutting it down so it'll fit nicely behind the seat.  My stereo is a work in progress ($$$$$)  As I get available money, I'll be getting new mids, and an amp to drive them, right now, all I have is the subwoofer upgrade.  And the deck I put in 2 years ago.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
